    "body": "Maintainer decision (owner's standing word 2026-11-22: choose recommended while he sleeps) - priority.\n\nThe test of the worker gives the three answers on `main` at `7c637d705`:\n\n1. The case is reachable: a retract height below the end of a higher run is accepted.\n2. The tool moves down into the part at the hop.\n3. The verifier blocks it: a `rapid_in_stock` finding and a 3.0 mm gouge finding, `blocks_post` true, and the gate is not ok. The post is held.\n\nSo no wrong program passes. By the priority table this is `P3` (wrong behaviour that a user finds, with a visible refusal), not `P1`.\n\n- Option 1 (taken, recommended): set `P3`, keep `effort:high`, keep the fix in the generator (the travel height of the plain hop is not below the end of the run), and keep an independent Opus read of the fix, because it changes emitted moves.\n- Option 2 (dropped): keep `P1`.\n\nPR #3625 is released from its hold: the question that held it has its answer. With `Pass starts at: Inside` on a convex part and such a retract height, the result is the same blocked post, not a silent gouge.\n\nFor the fix PR: correct the sentence in `docs/decisions/3362-pass-start-finish3d.md` that says each link \"is certified by the existing laws\" (it is not true for the plain hop before this fix).\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
